2331 0 obj
  << /ActualText (CAF\311 OVERVIEW\nName\072 Le Jardin de Sonia\050Owner\072 Sonia\050Established\072 2018 \050takeover of existing caf\351\051\050Status\072 Closing September 2026 \050due to legal dispute\051\n\nORIGIN \046 HISTORY\nInitial Acquisition \0502018\051\nPre\055existing caf\351 called \042Le Jardin\042 was running at the location\nFell in love with the place instantly upon visiting\nSonia heard about the availability from her hairdresser\nShe said that space was \042really ugly\042 initially and required transformation\nHer personal initiative \050not a family business\051\nKept original name \042Le Jardin\042 and added her own name\nRenovations \046 COVID Impact\n2020\054 two years after opening the COVID\05519 pandemic hit\noriginal space was too small for\072 take\055away food service \046 maintaining required social distancing\npost\055COVID renovation\072 expanded \057 transformed the caf\351 to accommodate more customers\n\nOWNER SONIA\072\nHer personal Collections in the Caf\351\nCoca\055Cola collection\072 Started collecting at age 15\073 includes bottles\054 posters\054 signs\054 cups\054 books\073 part of collection displayed in caf\351\054 rest at home\nphotos from her youth\054 childhood board games\nAll objects and interior elements from second\055hand shops and flea markets \222 create a colorful\054 wild\054 personal mix of interior\nHer Philosophy\nMotto\072 \042No rules\054 no stress\041\042 \222 No fixed routine\073 adapts daily to customer needs and flow\nValues showing love and care to customers\nTakes on multiple roles\072 caf\351 owner\054 social support\054 comfort provider\054 \042psychologist\042\054 friend\nProvides comfort and support when customers need it\n\nCUSTOMER RELATIONSHIPS\072\nDemographics\nAll age groups represented \222 strong intergenerational mixing\nPrimarily neighborhood clientele\nconstruction workers\054 writers\054 retirees\054 \056\056\056\nCommunity\nserves as neighborhood gathering place\nfacilitates intergenerational connections\nProvides consistent\054 familiar presence \050regular customers\054 predictable routines\051\nCreates sense of belonging and home away from home\nRelationship \057 Connection\ngoes beyond typical caf\351\055customer boundaries \222 notes that caf\351s typically maintain professional distance\054 but she intentionally doesn\047t\nRemembers customers\047 names and usual orders and asks if they want \042the same\042\nFriendship extends beyond caf\351 hours \222 social gatherings after closing \222 dinners\054 BBQ\057grill parties together\nCustomer Perception of the Place\072\n describe it as \042like entering a dollhouse\054 warm\054 sympathetic\042\nAnne \050regular customer\054 writer\051\072 Called it \042paradise\042\nAtmosphere described as like a \042living room\042 with home\055like feeling\nSo comfortable that customers sometimes forget to pay \050return in panic when they realize\051\n\nCUSTOMER STORIES\072\nRegular Morning Visitors\ntwo older women come every morning at 8\07200 AM\nsit in same spot \050back corner\051\054 always order\072 2 coffees and croissants\nunique behavior\072 Ask for second coffee before finishing the first\nhave Sonia\047s phone number\073 text her if they can\047t come so she won\047t worry\n Anne \050Writer\051\072\nComes frequently to the caf\351\nReserved the \042Wheel of Fortune\042 \050cardboard wheel with tasks\051 \222 special feature\072 wheel itself is spun\054 the pointer is static\nSonia joked she doesn\047t need ChatGPT\057AI for writing\054 she can ask Anne\nOlder man\072\nsolved a crossword riddle\nfound caf\351 randomly\nSecond visit observed during interview \222 already developed familiar\054 joking relationship with Sonia\nPatrick\072\ncomes regularly\nparticipated in the public holidays celebrated at the caf\351\nReconnection Moments\072\nCustomers who knew each other in the past but lost contact\nRandomly encounter each other at different tables in caf\351\nReconnect and move to sit together\nThese moments give Sonia \042goosebumps\042\nConflict Management\nOccasional conflicts when customers are very drunk\nSonia doesn\047t kick people out immediately \053 gives three chances if customers return\n\nBEVERAGES \046 SERVICE STYLE\nAttention to Craft\nCommon drinks \050e\056g\056\054 Aperol Spritz\051 made in special\054 visually appealing ways\nCoffee preparation\072 Values visible presentation\nClear layers of coffee and milk\nFeels proud of the visual result\nWants customers to see\057feel the care in preparation\nCocktail Customization\nActively encourages customers  to taste cocktails during preparation\nAllows for personalization based on customer feedback\n\nINTERIOR DESIGN\nOverall atmosphere\n\042Living room\042 aesthetic\024home atmosphere intentionally created\nEverything looks different \050sourced from various flea markets and second\055hand shops\051\nPersonal items integrated throughout\072 photos of young Sonia\054 board games from her childhood available\054 Coca\055Cola collection\nSpecial decoration  for public holidays \050example\072 everything red for St\056 Patrick\047s Day\051\nphoto album full of memories and events with customers\nTiteuf\nArtist\072 Zep \050creator of Titeuf comic\051\054 lives nearby\nPersonal connection\072 Same school as Sonia\nCharacters in comic based on real people from their school\nTiteuf character based on Zep himself\073 was in love with character Nadia\nReal Nadia has visited the caf\351\nWall drawings done in chalk\nSpecial Post\055It\072 \042Me to me\042 reserved for Sonia herself\nTiteuf comic books available in caf\351\nWill add protective layer before removing wallpaper\n\nINTERACTIVE ELEMENTS\nPost\055It\nOriginal location\072 Bathroom\nCustomers could write messages and put them on the walls\nSome appeared water\055damaged\057wet\nSonia collected them and compiled into a book\nCurrent use \050closure phase\051\072 Post\055Its now show \042Reserved \133name\135\042 throughout caf\351 \222 indicate who will receive specific interior and decoration elements after closure\nWheel of Fortune\nSelf\055made of cardboard\nContains tasks\nUnique feature\072 Wheel itself rotates \050not the pointer\051\nReserved by Anne \050regular customer\057writer\051\n\nSTAFF\072\nmultiple employee mentioned\nolder employee\072 Works Mondays and Fridays \222 more distant\057professional with customers \050contrast to Sonia\047s style\051\nall of them have their own luck pig for tips\n\nCURRENT CHALLENGES\072\nLegal Dispute \050Started 2022\051\nSonia purchased the caf\351 but doesn\047t fully own it\nOriginal\057older owner wants property back\nExtensive formal\057legal procedures ongoing\nEmotionally exhausting for Sonia\nRequired Changes\nMust restore caf\351 to original condition\nIncludes\072 lighting\054 walls\054 colors\054 and other modifications\nClosure Timeline\nClosing date\072 September 2024\nInterior elements being distributed to customers \050indicated by reservation Post\055Its\051\n\n\n\n\n\n)
