2389 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Put my notes in Claude\072\050\nMargaret\054 73\054 lives alone in a small apartment where the walls seem to grow closer each year\056 But every morning at 8\07215\054 she has a reason to brush her silver hair\054 put on her good cardigan\054 and step outside\056\n\nThe Bluebird Cafe\056\nHer corner table by the window\056 Her chamomile tea with exactly one sugar\056 Her toasted bread with butter\054 never jam\056 David\054 the owner\054 has her order ready before she reaches the counter\056 \042Morning\054 Margaret\056 Sleep well\077\042 It\047s the same question every day\054 and she cherishes it\056\nShe knows the regulars\056 Tom with his newspaper and black coffee\056 Sophie\054 the young artist who sketches in the back booth\056 They exchange small waves\054 brief conversations about the weather\054 the news\054 nothing and everything\056\nNext day\072 A sign says\072 CLOSING \055 FINAL MONTH\056\nWe jump forward\056 Margaret\047s bedroom\056 Afternoon light slices through dusty curtains\056 She hasn\047t gotten up\056 Why bother\077 The covers feel heavy\056 Her phone sits silent on the nightstand\056 No David asking about her sleep\056 No Sophie showing her drawings\056 Just walls\056 Just silence\056\nThe image blurs\024Margaret gasps awake in her armchair\054 hand clutched to her chest\056 It was a dream\056 A vision of the future\056 The cafe is still open\056 For now\056\nThe question\072 Will she make that call\077 Organize that petition\077 Fight for the one place that makes her feel alive\077)
