2397 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Dilemma of self\055care and being there for the neighbourhood\n\nThe weigh of warmth\077\n\nRosa knows every name\056 Every coffee order\056 Every birthday\056\nDawn breaks in her cafe and she\047s already there\054 hands dusted with cinnamon\054 piping the perfect rosette onto Mrs\056 Patel\047s cappuccino\056 She adds an extra chocolate curl to Leo\047s mocha because he mentioned a bad day yesterday\056 The croissants she shaped at 5 AM are golden\054 flaky miracles\056\nThe cafe glows\056 Sunlight pours through the windows\056 Customers linger over their cups\054 laughing\056 A student finds the courage to ask someone out\056 An elderly man makes a new friend\056 Rosa moves between tables like a conductor\054 her smile genuine every single time\056 \042How\047s your daughter\077\042 \042Did the interview go well\077\042 \042I saved you the corner seat\056\042\nShe is the heart that keeps this room beating\056\n\n10 PM\056 The door locks\056\nBlack and white\056 Silence\056 Rosa collapses into a chair\054 still wearing her apron\056 Bills spread across the table\024red ink everywhere\056 Her hands shake as she tries to count the register\056 Third month running at a loss\056\nThe espresso machine she can\047t afford to replace\056 The rent increase she can\047t afford to pay\056 The sleep she can\047t afford to lose\056\nHer phone buzzes\056 A regular asking if she\047ll be open tomorrow\056 She stares at it\054 tears blurring the screen\056\nThe question\072 How long can you pour from an empty cup\077\n)
     /K [ 389 ]
     /P 2398 0 R
     /Pg 1630 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
