  << /ActualText (From a Croissant\047s Perspective\056\nNo dilemma\077\n\nI am made of 231 layers\056 At 4 AM\054 Pierre\047s hands fold butter into dough\056 Fold\056 Rest\056 Fold\056 Rest\056 His father taught him this\056 His father\047s father before that\056 By 7 AM\054 I\047m golden in the display case\056 Pierre arranges me just so\054 tilting me toward the morning light\056 \nMadame Chen arrives\056 Every Thursday\056 Pierre already has me wrapped\054 knows her order by heart\056 She doesn\047t just buy me\024she cradles me in both palms\054 feeling my warmth\056 \042Still perfect\054 Pierre\056\042 \042For you\054 always\056\042\nShe takes me to the cemetery\056 Unwraps me slowly\056 Breaks off a piece and leaves it on her husband\047s headstone\056 Then she eats the rest\054 savoring every bite\054 telling him about her week\056 I taste like butter\054 yes\056 But also like fifty years of shared mornings\056)
