  << /ActualText (Perspective from the place itself \222 has personality\056\n\nIn the beginning empty\054 feels overlooked\054 people just pass by\054 wants a purpose\056\n\nThen \056\056\056 take the place \222 creates cafe\054 place is happy\056 owner has struggles \222 place fears to be lonely agaign\n\n\n\nFor the last decade\054 I\047ve been nothing\056 Empty\056 My windows dusty\056 My floors silent\056 People hurry past me every day\054 pulling their coats tighter\054 never looking up\056 I am just another vacant storefront\024overlooked\054 purposeless\054 slowly forgetting what it feels like to matter\056\n\nThen she comes\056 Lena stands at my door with paint samples and dreams\056 Her hands tremble as she unlocks me for the first time\056 She sweeps my floors\056 Washes my windows until light pours through\056 Hangs curtains that smell like lavender\056\n\nI am alive again\056 My walls hold laughter now\056 The espresso machine hisses like a heartbeat\056 Customers sink into the chairs Lena restored\054 telling each other their secrets\056 A couple gets engaged at my corner table\056 A writer finishes her novel in my window seat\056 Every morning\054 Lena arrives before dawn\054 and I feel her footsteps like a pulse\056\n\nBut then I feel it\024the shift\056 Lena\047s shoulders slumping\056 Bills piling on my counter\056 Her crying in my kitchen after close\054 head in her hands\056 The espresso machine breaks\056 She can\047t fix it\056 Customers trickle away\056\nOne night\054 she sits alone in the dark\054 staring at eviction notices\056\nI am terrified\056 I\047ve felt this before\024the slow drain of life\054 the gradual silence\056 I remember being empty\056 Forgotten\056 I cannot go back to that\056)
     /K [ 395 ]
     /P 2410 0 R
     /Pg 1630 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
