  << /ActualText (On the final day before the caf\351 closes\054 one of Sonia\031s most treasured objects slips from a shelf and shatters on the floor\056\050 For Sonia\054 the broken object feels like proof that some things cannot be preserved\054 no matter how much they are loved\056\n\050 But Tom\054 a customer visiting for the first time\054 sees the accident differently \055 not as an ending\054 but as something still worth saving \055 and proposes to take the object home and repair it himself\056\n\050 As Sonia shares the story behind the piece and the collection it once belonged to\054 the two begin confronting different ways of facing loss\072 accepting disappearance or trying to hold onto what remains\056\n\050 When Tom returns the next day with the restored object in his hands\054 the question still lingers between them\072 can something truly survive once the place that gave it meaning is gone\077)
