2521 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Empty Chair\n\nMarko arrives at Sabine\047s Cafe every morning at 7\07243 AM\056 Not 7\07240\056 Not 7\07245\056 7\07243\056\nThe bell above the door chimes\054 and Sabine is already pouring black coffee\054 two sugars\054 hot enough to need three minutes of cooling\056 She sets it on the corner table by the window\056 His table\056 His chair\054 the one with the slight wobble he claims he likes because \042it keeps you honest\056\042 They don\047t talk much\056 \042Morning\054 Marko\056\042 \042Morning\054 Sabine\056\042 Sometimes he mentions the weather\056 Sometimes she asks about his garden\056 But mostly\054 they exist in comfortable silence\024the kind that only comes after years of showing up for each other\056 He stays for exactly one hour\056 Reads the paper\056 Watches the neighborhood wake up\056 Leaves a five\055dollar bill under his saucer\054 same as always\054 though the coffee only costs three\056 For twelve years\054 this has been their dance\056\n\nTuesday\054 7\07243 AM\056 The door doesn\047t open\056 Sabine glances at the clock\056 Pours the coffee anyway\056 Maybe he\047s running late\056 By 8\07200\054 the coffee has gone cold\056 She dumps it\054 feels foolish for the tightness in her chest\056\n\nWednesday\054 7\07243 AM\056 Nothing\056 She calls his cell\056 Straight to voicemail\056 Calls again\056 Again\056 Her hands shake as she wipes down tables that don\047t need wiping\056\n\nThursday morning\054 she stops pretending to work\056 She gathers the regulars\024Sophie\054 James\054 Mrs\056 Patel\054 the book club ladies\056 \042Something\047s wrong\056\042 They don\047t question her\056 They know\056 When someone is woven into your daily rhythm for twelve years\054 you feel the absence like a missing heartbeat\056\n\nSabine flips the sign to CLOSED\024first time in a decade\024and they scatter across the neighborhood\056 Knocking on Marko\047s door\056 Calling hospitals\056 Checking with neighbors who barely knew his name\056 It\047s Sophie who finds him\056 Collapsed in his kitchen\056 Alone for two days\056 \n\nCare isn\047t always loud\056 Sometimes it\047s just black coffee at 7\07243 AM\054 ready before you walk through the door\056\nSometimes noticing is everything)
     /K [ 451 ]
     /P 2522 0 R
     /Pg 1630 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
