2567 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Baked Fragments\240\nKostas KATKEVICIUS\054 Carla No\353lle MARTINI\054 Luca CORREIA DA ROCHA\n\nV1\nOn the final day before her caf\351 closes\054 one of Monika\031s most treasured objects slips from a shelf and shatters on the floor\056\050 Not wanting the sadness of the moment to disturb the warmth of the caf\351\054 she quietly hides the broken pieces behind the counter\056\050 Tom\054 a customer visiting for the very first time\054 gently proposes to take the object home and repair it himself\056\050 As Sonia tells him its story\054 he realises the object is part of a collection that had silently shaped the soul of the place for years \072 they were brought here by faithful customers\054 because here\054 in this caf\351\054 they feel at home\056\050 The next day\054 Tom returns with the restored object in his hands \055 as if trying to save a small piece of the caf\351 before it disappears forever\056\240\n\nV2\nMonika\047s caf\351 walls hold twenty years of gifts\054 each one placed there by a customer who called this their second living room\056 Tom\054 visiting for the first time\054 watches her move between tables with such warmth and passion\054 that he understands immediately\072 this isn\047t a business\054 it\047s a family\056 Then Monika\047s hand slips and Mrs\056 Barbara\047s porcelain teddy bear shatters against the floor\054 she sweeps the pieces behind the counter with shaking hands\054 but Tom has already seen the grief\054 and though he\047s a stranger here\054 he feels the urge to offer help for an object that reminds to Monika the presence of the most loyal customer that is not there anymore\056\n\n\240\n\024\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nFeedback V2\nLoyalty stood out \023 are they really loyal or it is more about something else \050surprised about this loyalty\051\nWhich perspective do we wanna take\077 Tell from Monikas \050owner\051 or Toms \050customer\051 point of view\077\nTell the story from the perspective of the broken object\077\nPersons inside of the caf\351 stood out as being a more important aspect as the caf\350 itself \050Family\051\nConnection between people as the core element\nWhat is Monika doing in the beginning\077\nHow does Monika think about her customers\077\nDo the words passion and warmth connect to each other to express Monika\031s personality\077\240\n\034 to offer help for an object that reminds Monika the presence of the most loyal customer that is not there anymore \034 \055 this sentence felt not understood by the crowd\056\240\n\nWhat are we planning to do in order to respond to the feedback\072\n\nNot rewrite the story from scratch \072\051\nShift focus from the loyalty aspect\nChoose a specific perspective from which the story will be told\056 To be more concrete\056\nShift the focus from Loyalty to another emotion\056 \050for example\072 openness\054 peacefulness\054 gratefulness\054 happiness\054 comfort \055 second home\051\nStrengthen the setting of the story\054 so that it becomes THE SPECIAL PLACE \050this should be seen and understood\051\nReplace the last phrase or delete it completely\056 \050to offer help for an object that reminds Monika the presence of the most loyal customer that is not there anymore\051\nMaybe hint very subtly that the caf\350 will shut down\056\240\nAdd more context to the story \050in 3 sentences it is not manageable\051 in order to support the fact that someone passed away\056\n\nMake sure that the caf\351 still here so the story can not be in another settings\nHow do we give visitors the feeling of walking into a welcoming space \057 community\n\n\nFind some non demanding way to contribute to the story telling\056 Choosing something\054 recording their memory\056 Spontaneously contribute\056\240\n\nGo with the book and see what they remember from the book and if they remember something\054 you could choose your favourite page in this book and ask something about that\056\240\n\nDo we go deeper into the photo book\077\nTension \055\076 Person struggling\054 what are her limits\054 fears\077 Grow from limits or break\077 Tension more in the closing of the cafe\077\n\nWhat people are going to do in their free time after the Jardin de Sonia will close\077\240\n\nSomething to attach to get into the story\077\n\050)
     /K [ 474 ]
